son`. Pre-revision and reserved-hardened inputs can't be produced, so old entries miss rather than alias.\n- **Worker boundary** — identity-verified hidden-mode re-execution of the manager (`cmd/curator __curator-go-worker-v1`), nonce-bound `list` → parent graph validation → HMAC-authenticated permit → `build`, with pre-launch, in-session and post-exec identity checks and full domain teardown.\n- **Native controls** — `rc5-native-control-inventory-v1` probed once per operation before launch; macOS `setsid` + `RLIMIT_FSIZE` + close-on-exec, Windows Job Object kill-on-close/active-process/memory + explicit handle list. Closed `capability-evidence-v1` record with all eight consistency rules, result-only.\n- **Deferred guarantees** — the six hardened names appear nowhere and never reject.\n\n## Evidence\n\nGreen on three native hosts: macOS arm64 (incl. `-race`), macOS amd64 (`ssh relux`), Windows amd64 (`ssh win`) — each with a real Go 1.25.5 vendored build that is verified and never started. 222 cases pass under the rc.5 conformance root. Scoped `golangci-lint` exits 0 with 0 issues.\n\n## Reported red, not fixed\n\n- `go test ./...` on Windows exits 1 on five packages this task doesn't own (`buildcache`, `buildsource`, `globalbins`, `runtimestore`, `shell`) — POSIX exec-bit and Windows ownership/rename assumptions. All green on both macOS hosts; all fail before any go-v1 code runs. First native Windows full-suite run exposed them.\n- Whole-repository `golangci-lint run` exits 1 with 45 pre-existing findings elsewhere; no green claimed for it or the Makefile `lint` target.\n- Linux runtime is honestly deferred — the inventory covers only macOS and Windows, so Linux rejects with `build_execution_control_unavailable` before the worker. Coverage there is compile/vet/test-link plus that rejection path.\n\nTwo findings worth flagging: `RLIMIT_FSIZE` proved itself by *breaking* tests that set the bound too low, and `filepath.IsAbs(\"/etc/passwd\")` is false on Windows — a r